 ### Mathematical Morphology on Voxelization
-This variant extends dilation to include erosion and supports separable operations for efficiency [S2, unofficial]. In a binary context, erosion and dilation are logical AND/OR operations. They are separable, meaning one can first erode/dilate along the x and y directions, then along the z direction [S2, unofficial]. Larger kernel sizes are achieved by iterating the operation. This approach allows arbitrary rectangular kernels and uses bit-shifting to treat columns efficiently, though care must be taken with bits spanning adjacent integers [S2, unofficial]. It is faster than lengthy preprocesses because it relies solely on the solid voxelization as the only step involving actual scene geometry, making it purely image-based [S2, unofficial].
